  {
   "id": "id-api-97",
   "identifier": "API-97",
   "title": "Slow /reports endpoint for large workspaces",
   "url": "https://linear.app/acme/issue/API-97",
   "description": "## TL;DR\n\nOn Monday the `/v1/reports` endpoint took **8 to 12 seconds** for workspaces with more than 500 reports. The query scans every report of the workspace because there is **no index on `(workspace_id, updated_at)`**. The 500s from empty dashboards are a different bug, fixed in [API-91](https://linear.app/acme/issue/API-91/api-returns-500-for-a-dashboard-with-no-widgets).\n\n## Timeline (Monday)\n\n| Time | What |\n| -- | -- |\n| ~09:10 | First customer report in support: the reports page spins for about 10 seconds. |\n| 09:40 | p95 latency alert fires for `GET /v1/reports`. It flaps for an hour and nobody picks it up. |\n| 11:05 | Root cause found: a full scan of `reports` for large workspaces ([acme/api#207](https://github.com/acme/api/pull/207) only fixed the 500s). |\n| 12:30 | Hotfix merged: page size capped at 100 ([acme/web#318](https://github.com/acme/web/pull/318)). |\n\n## Why it is slow\n\n- The list query sorts by `updated_at` but filters by `workspace_id`, and neither column is indexed together.\n- Every page re-counts all reports for the total, so page 2 costs as much as page 1.\n- Large workspaces grew from 200 to 800 reports in the last quarter, so this got worse *without any code change*.\n\n## Asks\n\n1. **Index:** add `(workspace_id, updated_at)` and check the plan with `EXPLAIN ANALYZE`.\n2. **Count:** cache the total per workspace for 60 seconds instead of counting on every page.\n3. **Alert:** route the p95 alert to the API team's channel, so it is not missed again.\n",
   "updatedAt": "@-300",
   "createdAt": "@-4000",
   "priority": 3,
   "state": {
    "id": "team-api-review",
    "name": "In Review",
    "color": "#0f783c",
    "position": 5,
    "type": "started"
   },
   "team": {
    "id": "team-api"
   },
   "assignee": {
    "name": "Alex Kim"
   },
   "creator": {
    "name": "Jo Doe"
   },
   "parent": null,
   "project": null,
   "attachments": {
    "nodes": [
